        },
        "accordion_cNMQDg": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "name": "FAQs accordians",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "caret",
            "dividers": true,
            "type_preset": "h5",
            "inherit_color_scheme": true,
            "color_scheme": "",
            "border": "none",
            "border_width": 1,
            "border_opacity": 100,
            "border_radius": 0,
            "padding-block-start": 0,
            "padding-block-end": 0,
            "padding-inline-start": 0,
            "padding-inline-end": 0
          },
          "blocks": {
            "accordion_row_hhKbAV": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "name": "t:names.accordion_row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Unified inventory",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_XH4zWU": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>HotWax syncs real-time inventory data from your ERP, WMS, POS and calculates Available to Promise (ATP) inventory, which can actually be sold online. It subtracts inventory held as safety stock, thresholds, already committed to open orders, or unavailable for online sale, leaving only the truly sellable quantity to sync with eCommerce platforms, preventing oversells and unnecessary cancellations.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "color": "var(--color-foreground)",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_XH4zWU"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_BeFmNh": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "name": "t:names.accordion_row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Estimated delivery date on the PDP",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_RBRABV": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>HotWax calculates estimated delivery dates using the customer’s location. When a shopper enters their zip code or allows browser location, HotWax captures the latitude and longitude of that address. Each fulfillment location’s coordinates are also stored in the OMS. Using these coordinates, HotWax compares the distance between the customer and nearby fulfillment locations and displays an estimated delivery date based on the closest location with available inventory.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "color": "var(--color-foreground)",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_RBRABV"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_RKbwKf": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "name": "t:names.accordion_row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Mixed carts",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_xPjyGc": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>HotWax lets customers combine shipping and pickup items in the same order and clearly labels which items are for delivery and which are for store pickup.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "color": "var(--color-foreground)",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_xPjyGc"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_UCwGEL": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Order routing",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_MpGFxq": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>HotWax intelligent order routing routes online orders to the best fulfillment location based on factors such as shipping method, promised SLA, proximity to the customer's address, inventory levels, fulfillment capacity and more.</p><p></p><p>HotWax’s order routing automatically selects the best fulfillment location for each order. The routing engine evaluates factors such as proximity to the customer, promised SLA, inventory levels, and fulfillment capacity to decide where the order should be fulfilled.<br/><br/>Retailers can define routing rules to prioritize certain locations, such as warehouses first and stores as backup, or nearby stores for same-day and next-day deliveries. If the preferred location cannot fulfill the order, the routing engine automatically checks the next best location to keep orders moving without manual intervention.<br/><br/>Routing can also control order splits. Orders are fulfilled from a single location whenever possible, and are only split when necessary to meet delivery promises.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "color": "var(--color-foreground)",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_MpGFxq"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_gyAGix": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "name": "t:names.accordion_row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Order splitting",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_pq9dpw": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Split orders only when needed. For same-day or next-day delivery promises, HotWax's routing engine intelligently splits orders across multiple locations if a single location cannot fulfill the entire order.</p><p>To protect your margins, you can set a minimum shipment threshold value. This means split shipments are avoided for low-value order items, keeping delivery costs firmly under control while still delivering a premier customer experience.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "color": "var(--color-foreground)",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_pq9dpw"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_FprLLA": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "name": "t:names.accordion_row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Product based routing",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_EBLnti": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Automatically route order items with custom fulfillment steps like engraving or alterations from locations that support those services.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "color": "var(--color-foreground)",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_EBLnti"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_yRd3HR": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "name": "t:names.accordion_row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Handle new launches",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_C9krYU": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>HotWax's configurable routing engine protects the in-store experience during major product drops. By initially routing online orders for high-demand items strictly to warehouses, online orders won't wipe out store inventory. Stores are only used for fulfillment once demand stabilizes, so that walk-in customers find stocked shelves.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "color": "var(--color-foreground)",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_C9krYU"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_jRWGkc": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Order fulfillment in stores",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_T7giax": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>HotWax's lightweight Fulfillment App makes store fulfillment simple for staff. Store associates can pick orders in batches and sort them by shipping method to meet tight SLAs. Guided picklists show exactly what to pick and from where, while barcode scanning and full-size product images help reduce mistakes during picking.<br/><br/>For shipping, HotWax automatically rate shops across carriers to choose the most cost-effective option that still meets the delivery SLA. Labels can be printed in advance, orders are automatically marked as shipped with tracking codes, and tracking details are synced across systems and sent to customers automatically.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "color": "var(--color-foreground)",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_T7giax"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_aMkV4T": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Order fulfillment capacity",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_dtr3XX": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Set daily order caps to prevent store teams from being overloaded during peak periods. </p><p>You can also deprioritize stores with heavy walk-in traffic, such as mall locations, to protect the in-store experience.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "color": "var(--color-foreground)",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_dtr3XX"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_6JgQaL": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "name": "t:names.accordion_row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Special orders",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_ft94Rw": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "name": "t:names.text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Store staff can fulfill kit products and service-based items, such as gift packs or bundled products. Even though kits contain multiple components, the Fulfillment App guides associates on what items need to be picked and packed so the bundle is fulfilled correctly.</p><p>The Fulfillment App also supports gift card activation. When a gift card order is processed, store staff can activate it directly through the app.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
